---
/**
 * Privacy-friendly analytics — Plausible.
 *
 * Gated by env var `PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN`. When empty/unset, NO script
 * is emitted, no network call is made, no third-party connection happens.
 * That keeps preview deploys / local dev free of analytics noise.
 *
 * To activate in prod:
 *   1. Create the site on plausible.io with domain = com-compass.com
 *   2. Set PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=com-compass.com in the build env
 *      (Vercel: Project Settings → Env Vars · GCP: GHA workflow env)
 *   3. Redeploy. The `<script>` tag below activates automatically.
 *
 * Script variant used: `script.outbound-links.js` — also tracks clicks on
 * outbound links (mailto:, external) which is exactly what we need for the
 * `mailto:contact@com-compass.com` CTA conversion funnel.
 *
 * ⚠️ TURNING THIS ON IS A LEGAL CHANGE, NOT A CONFIG CHANGE.
 *
 * The published privacy policy states, in § 8 and in the affirmative:
 * "Nous ne déposons aucun traceur de mesure d'audience non exemptée, de
 * publicité ou de suivi tiers." That sentence is true today precisely because
 * `PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN` is unset and this script is never emitted.
 *
 * Setting the variable makes the page load a script from a third-party origin.
 * Before doing so:
 *   1. have counsel confirm the deployment qualifies for the consent exemption
 *      of art. 82 of loi n° 78-17 — vendor claims are not a CNIL position, and
 *      Plausible is not on the CNIL's published exemption list;
 *   2. update § 8 of /confidentialite/ and /en/privacy/ accordingly;
 *   3. if it is not exempt, ship a consent banner FIRST. Trackers are the
 *      CNIL's largest financial-risk category.
 *
 * Enabling it and leaving the policy as written does not merely create a
 * breach — it documents one, in our own words, with a date.
 */
const domain = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN as string | undefined;
const enabled = typeof domain === 'string' && domain.length > 0;
---

{enabled && (
  <script
    is:inline
    defer
    data-domain={domain}
    src="https://plausible.io/js/script.outbound-links.js"
  ></script>
)}
